WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.260
Fire And Blood will reign again and you can
expect to see the Blackfyre Rebellions in

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.880
the later seasons of House of the Dragon!
The upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series,

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:26.060
House of the Dragon, is based on the George
RR Martin's Targaryen history book Fire &amp; Blood.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:30.750
House of the Dragon is a Game of Thrones prequel
show that is confirmed by HBO’s president

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.850
to air in 2022.
Miguel Sapochnik and Ryan Condal will serve

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:40.120
as showrunners and executive producers. George
R. R. Martin will also serve as executive

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.180
producer.
It is based on George RR Martin’s book Fire

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:48.760
And Blood volume 1 and on Martin’s yet unfinished
Fire And Blood volume 2 book.

00:00:48.760 --> 00:00:53.100
“Fire &amp; Blood begins their tale with the
legendary Aegon the Conqueror, creator of

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:57.809
the Iron Throne, and goes on to recount the
generations of Targaryens who fought to hold

00:00:57.809 --> 00:01:02.930
that iconic seat, all the way up to the civil
war that nearly tore their dynasty apart.”

00:01:02.930 --> 00:01:07.580
In other words it covers events from Aegon's
Conquest to the Dance of the Dragons.

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:11.170
That's Fire And Blood volume 1.
House of the Dragon will start with a build

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:16.350
up towards the Dance of the Dragons
and early seasons will cover the Dance itself.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.440
Later seasons however,
will be based on George RR Martin’s yet

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:24.360
unfinished Fire And Blood volume 2 book .
The yet unreleased Fire And Blood volume 2

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:30.080
will continue from where part 1 ended, with
Rhaenyra Targaryen's son Aegon lll's reign

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:35.400
and will cover Blackyre rebellions, war with
Dorne and go all the way to the Mad King and

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.539
Robert's Rebellion that ended Targaryen dynasty.
How do I know the second part of the Targaryen

00:01:40.539 --> 00:01:45.280
history will cover all of that?
Because George RR Martin himself revealed

00:01:45.280 --> 00:02:32.209
it.
Fire And Blood volume 1 has 700 pages.

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:35.500
In comparison, the book material Game of Thrones
show used

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:41.280
was 4000 pages with the additional summary
from George RR Martin about the ending.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:45.670
This prequel will last at least as long as
Game of Thrones and to achieve that,

00:02:45.670 --> 00:02:50.390
the showrunners will use Fire And Blood volume
2 material and as I already said,

00:02:50.390 --> 00:02:54.780
the main events of it are the Blackfyre Rebellions
and the Robert's Rebellion

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:59.409
so this is something you will see on screen
in the later seasons of House of the Dragon.

00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:02.890
The First Blackfyre Rebellion, originally
called the Blackfyre Rebellion,

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:07.819
was a war fought between the loyalist forces
of King Daeron II Targaryen

00:03:07.819 --> 00:03:12.040
and the rebel forces of his half-brother,
Daemon I Blackfyre.

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:18.489
Daemon I Blackfyre, born Daemon Waters, was
a bastard son of King Aegon IV Targaryen

00:03:18.489 --> 00:03:23.409
and Princess Daena Targaryen. Legitimized
by his father upon the latter's death,

00:03:23.409 --> 00:03:28.150
Daemon took the name "Blackfyre" for himself,
after the ancestral Valyrian steel sword of

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:32.579
House Targaryen, which his father also bequeathed
to him.

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:37.340
Despite his bastard status, Daemon believed
himself the rightful heir to the Iron Throne,

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:42.689
as his father's firstborn (and favorite) child
and ignited a bloody civil war that divided

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:47.819
the Seven Kingdoms against his half-brother
Daeron II Targaryen. But let's get a bit back

00:03:47.819 --> 00:03:52.879
to see how it all started.
After King Baelor I Targaryen made peace with

00:03:52.879 --> 00:03:57.840
Dorne, he returned to King's Landing
and annulled his marriage to his eldest sister,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:01.029
Daena.
He then locked Daena so she could not tempt

00:04:01.029 --> 00:04:04.769
the lusts of men.
However, Daena escaped her imprisonment on

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:07.810
several occasions,
and towards the end of her brother's reign

00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:14.450
became pregnant by her cousin, Prince Aegon.
In late 170 AC, she gave birth to a bastard

00:04:14.450 --> 00:04:20.250
son whom she named Daemon Waters.
Baelor I, in response to Daemon's birth, began

00:04:20.250 --> 00:04:26.100
a forty-day fast,
which eventually caused his death in 171 AC.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:30.940
King Aegon IV Targaryen, ascended the Iron
Throne in 172 AC.

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:34.610
In addition to his unacknowledged bastard
son by Daena,

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:38.720
King Aegon IV Targaryen had by his marriage
to his sister, Naerys,

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:45.870
a trueborn son named Daeoron, born in 153
AC, and a daughter, Daenerys, born in 172

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:48.740
AC.
Aegon often clashed with Prince Daeron during

00:04:48.740 --> 00:04:53.970
his reign, with Daeron opposing the ideas
and the corrupt style of rule of his father.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:05:00.220
Aegon, on the other hand, despised his sister-wife,
Naerys, and his younger brother, Prince Aemon

00:05:00.220 --> 00:05:04.060
the Dragonknight, to both of whom Prince Daeron
was close.

00:05:04.060 --> 00:05:09.200
Around the same time, rumors began to circulate,
instigated by King Aegon himself,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:15.340
that Daeron was a bastard born of adultery
between his siblings, Naerys and Aemon.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:20.190
For the first time, although not the last,
Aegon threatened to name one of his bastard

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:26.320
sons as his heir over Daeron. The rumors about
Daeron's parentage forever remained, but despite

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.530
Aegon's threats and japes, Daeron was never
formally disowned.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:35.980
Meanwhile, two factions began to form at court,
one supporting the corrupt reign of Aegon

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:42.560
IV, the other supporting Daeron.
In 182 AC, Aegon knighted his bastard son,

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.840
Daemon Waters,
after the boy won a squire's tourney at the

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:52.200
age of twelve. Aegon publicly bestowed Blackfyre,
one of the Valyrian steel swords of House

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:57.720
Targaryen, on Daemon as well, finally acknowledging
him. There were some who felt that the sword

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:01.072
symbolized the monarchy
as it had been the sword of King Aegon I Targaryen,

00:06:01.072 --> 00:06:05.600
the Conqueror,
and had been passed on from king to king ever

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.820
since.
Aegon's public gift of the sword eventually

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:14.181
started the talk that Daemon should be king.
Following the acquisition of the sword, Daemon

00:06:14.181 --> 00:06:20.920
took the name "Blackfyre" for himself.
In early 184 AC, King Aegon IV Targaryen legitimized

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:25.640
all of his bastards on his deathbed.
Prince Daeron ascended the throne as King

00:06:25.640 --> 00:06:29.880
Daeron II Targaryen,
and did all he could to keep the nobly-born

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.950
Great Bastards close.
While Daeron had chosen to be crowned with

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:38.470
his father's crown, rumors about his legitimacy
remained.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:43.290
Daeron was not a warrior, and while Prince
Baelor, Daeron's eldest son by his Dornish

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:46.160
wife,
was all that could be desired in a warrior,

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:51.710
Baelor had the looks of a Martell,
and not, like Daemon Blackfyre, of a Targaryen.

00:06:51.710 --> 00:06:56.830
Nobles and knights from the Dornish Marches
began to mistrust both Daeron and Baelor.

00:06:56.830 --> 00:07:02.720
These same people looked at Daemon Blackfyre,
the bastard son of King Aegon IV Targaryen

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:09.060
and his cousin, Princess Daena Targaryen,
and saw in him a warrior, grown tall and powerful,

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:14.730
with the hallmarks of Old Valyria (deep purple
eyes, silver-gold hair down to his shoulders),

00:07:14.730 --> 00:07:20.530
who was described as having had an "almost
inhumane beauty", being "half a god among

00:07:20.530 --> 00:07:24.320
mortal men".
Daemon had come to resemble Aegon the Conqueror

00:07:24.320 --> 00:07:30.140
in appearance according to his supporters.
His armor was ornate and costly, all black

00:07:30.140 --> 00:07:34.320
and red plate,
and his war helm was distinctive, with batlike

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:38.920
steel "dragon wings" on the sides.
Daemon matured into a man of considerable

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:43.930
charm and strength, mastering all weapons
of the battlefield, but with the sword Blackfyre

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:47.580
in hand he was said to fight like the Warrior
himself.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:51.140
He won friends easily and women were drawn
to him.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:57.020
Married to Rohanne of Tyrosh in 184 AC, his
twin sons Aegon and Aemon were born later

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:03.380
that same year. Six other sons, and at least
two daughters followed during the years to

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:06.280
come.
Daemon's supporters claimed that Daemon had

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:12.490
desired his half-sister, Princess Daenerys,
and the singers claim that she loved him as

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:16.610
well. It is said that Aegon, who had seen
more profit in the match with Tyrosh, had

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:20.020
promised Daemon that he could have more than
one bride.

00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:25.240
Daeron, however did not agree. The Dornish
concessions and influence,

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:30.970
the sudden change of Dornish enemies to Dornish
allies, Daeron's rumored illegitimacy,

00:08:30.970 --> 00:08:36.430
and Aegon IV's public gift of the sword of
kings to Daemon, all were part the seeds from

00:08:36.430 --> 00:08:41.550
which the first Blackfyre Rebellion grew.
Still, it took many years for the actual rebellion

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:45.029
to begin.
There was no final insult that resulted in

00:08:45.029 --> 00:08:49.620
declaration of Daemon's claim.
Additionally, he had councilors who urged

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:53.310
him to rebel,
and many famous warriors who disagreed with

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:58.339
the peace with Dorne sought him out.
The First Blackfyre Rebellion finally broke

00:08:58.339 --> 00:09:03.330
out in 196 AC.
It lasted almost one year and divided the

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:08.910
Seven Kingdoms. Daemon's decision to claim
the throne had been made rashly, and word

00:09:08.910 --> 00:09:13.839
soon reached Daeron's court that Daemon meant
to declare within a month. It has been suggested

00:09:13.839 --> 00:09:19.930
by Archmaester Merion that Brynden Rivers,
another one of Aegon IV's bastard sons, (who

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:24.470
later went on to become the Three Eyed Raven
and who we met 100 years later in Game of

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:28.300
Thrones) was involved in the news reaching
Daeron.

00:09:28.300 --> 00:09:32.920
The Kingsguard was sent to arrest Daemon,
but, with the aid of the master-at-arms of

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:39.300
the Red Keep, Daemon managed to escape imprisonment.
Daemon reversed the colors of House Targaryen,

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:44.660
taking for his own sigil a black dragon on
a red field, which led to his nickname,

00:09:44.660 --> 00:09:48.740
the "black dragon" (with Daeron becoming known
as the "red dragon"),

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:53.740
and began to mint his own coinage.
Over the course of the war, battles were fought

00:09:53.740 --> 00:09:59.089
between the rebels and loyalists in amongst
other places, the Vale, the westerlands, the

00:09:59.089 --> 00:10:03.470
riverlands and the Reach. Half the realm declared
for Daemon.

00:10:03.470 --> 00:10:08.790
Ser Quentyn Ball attacked the westerlands,
killing Lord Lefford at the gates of Lannisport

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.990
and then defeating Lord Damon Lannister in
turn.

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:17.180
Lord Leo Tyrell participated in the First
Blackfyre Rebellion as well, fighting on behalf

00:10:17.180 --> 00:10:22.639
of House Targaryen. He won notable victories
in the Reach against Daemon Blackfyre's supporters.

00:10:22.639 --> 00:10:28.199
A key general, Fireball was slain on the eve
of the battle of the Redgrass Field by a common

00:10:28.199 --> 00:10:31.259
archer.
The final conflict of the First Blackfyre

00:10:31.259 --> 00:10:36.600
Rebellion was the Battle of the Redgrass Field,
in late 196 AC.

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:41.490
Lord Leo Tyrell's forces could not gather
quickly enough to arrive in time for the battle.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:47.510
House Arryn did participate, as Lord Donnel
Arryn led the vanguard of the Targaryen forces.

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:53.170
However, Daemon Blackfyre shattered his lines,
leaving the loyalists in peril until Ser Gwayne

00:10:53.170 --> 00:10:59.510
Corbray of the Kingsguard arrived with reinforcements.
Ser Gwayne Corbray and Daemon Blackfyre came

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:04.170
face-to-face during the battle.
Their epic duel, in which Daemon wielded the

00:11:04.170 --> 00:11:08.920
Valyrian steel sword Blackfyre
and Gwayne the Valyrian steel sword Lady Forlorn,

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:14.079
is said to have lasted nearly an hour
before Daemon gained the upper hand. Corbray

00:11:14.079 --> 00:11:19.570
was wounded, but Daemon dismounted,
preventing Corbray from being trampled, and

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:24.770
commanded that he was taken off the field.
While Daemon was doing this honorable deed,

00:11:24.770 --> 00:11:29.970
his half-brother Brynden Rivers with his archers,
the Raven's Teeth, had captured and assumed

00:11:29.970 --> 00:11:34.749
a position atop the Weeping Ridge,
which overlooked the battlefield and allowed

00:11:34.749 --> 00:11:40.949
them to rain arrows down among Daemon and
his commanders. Daemon’s heir Aegon died

00:11:40.949 --> 00:11:45.050
first, followed by Daemon himself.
When Daemon’s second son, Aegon’s twin

00:11:45.050 --> 00:11:48.880
brother Aemon took up Blackfyre, he was slain
as well.

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:54.999
With Daemon dead, the rebels began to rout.
Aegor Rivers claimed Blackfyre and rallied

00:11:54.999 --> 00:11:58.350
the rebels
by leading a charge against the Raven's Teeth,

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:02.809
but was eventually forced to flee
when Prince Baelor arrived with a host of

00:12:02.809 --> 00:12:07.629
Dornish spearmen and stormlanders,
while his younger brother, Prince Maekar,

00:12:07.629 --> 00:12:12.259
rallied what remained of the van.
As such, Baelor crushed the rebel army against

00:12:12.259 --> 00:12:15.939
Maekar’s shield wall,
the move later called “the hammer and the

00:12:15.939 --> 00:12:19.240
anvil”.
Ten thousand men died, and many more were

00:12:19.240 --> 00:12:23.209
maimed and wounded.
The First Blackfyre Rebellion left its mark

00:12:23.209 --> 00:12:27.579
upon Westeros for years to come.
Asking a man whether he had fought for the

00:12:27.579 --> 00:12:33.319
black dragon or the red was considered a dangerous
question. Aegor Rivers was able to recover

00:12:33.319 --> 00:12:38.329
the sword Blackfyre from the battlefield and
escaped to the Free Cities, together with

00:12:38.329 --> 00:12:42.699
Daemon's widow and remaining children, eventually
ending up in Tyrosh.

00:12:42.699 --> 00:12:47.220
In exile, Daemon's descendants continued their
struggle for the Iron Throne,

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:52.249
resulting in four more rebellions (Second,
Third and Fourth Blackfyre Rebellion, and

00:12:52.249 --> 00:12:58.139
the War of the Ninepenny Kings). These attempts
led to the arrest of Daemon's second son (Daemon),

00:12:58.139 --> 00:13:03.080
and the deaths of his third and fifth son
(Haegon and Aenys), as well as the death of

00:13:03.080 --> 00:13:07.559
a grandson,
also named Daemon. Daemon's last male descendant,

00:13:07.559 --> 00:13:13.920
Maelys, was slain during the War of the Ninepenny
Kings by Ser Barristan Selmy, ending the Blackfyre

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:17.199
threat.
That's the story of the Blackfyre Rebellion.

00:13:17.199 --> 00:13:19.870
Thank you so much for watching, I hope you
enjoyed this video and if you did please give

00:13:19.870 --> 00:13:27.969
it a big thumbs up and I hope to see you in
the next one. Peace!

